---
title: Salmon with spinach, feta and sweet potatoes
servings: 4
tags: [greek, weeknight]
cuisine: greek
time: 55 minutes
source: Sheet Pan Salmon with Spinach, Feta & Sweet Potatoes by Diane Kochilas, https://www.dianekochilas.com/sheet-pan-salmon-with-spinach-feta-sweet-potatoes
---

Heat the oven to 350°F.

Rinse the @salmon steaks{4}(bone-in) and pat them dry.

Whisk the juice of @lemon{1}(strained), @honey{1%tbsp}, @dijon mustard{2%tsp}, @olive oil{3%tbsp}, @salt{} and @ground black pepper{}. Turn the salmon in it and leave it to marinate while you do the vegetables.

In a large bowl, mix the @red onion{1}(finely chopped), @garlic{3%cloves}(minced), @leeks{2}(trimmed, chopped), @baby spinach{8%cups}, @dill{1%bunch}(chopped), @sweet potatoes{3}(peeled, in 1 1/2-inch chunks), the zest of @lemon{1/2}, @feta{1%cup}(crumbled), a little more @olive oil{}, salt and pepper.

Spread the vegetables in a large #glass baking dish{}. Lay the salmon on top, pour over any marinade left in the bowl, and scatter over the @feta{1/2%cup}.

Cover with #parchment paper{} and then foil, and bake ~{35%minutes}, until the salmon flakes and the vegetables are soft.

> Wild fennel fronds can stand in for the dill. A Greek pine honey is good here.
